              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.CHECK_STAGE.$output.resolvedQuestion}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"answer\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The response text to show the user\"\n    },\n    \"foundInDocuments\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\",\n      \"description\": \"true if the answer is grounded in the attached document tool\"\n    },\n    \"isActiveIncident\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\",\n      \"description\": \"true if the user's question described a live or ongoing incident rather than a general policy question, prompting reporting steps guidance instead of a standard answer\"\n    },\n    \"sources\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"description\": \"The files that ground this answer. Empty if foundInDocuments is false. Never contains the document tool's own name or code.\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"fileName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"The exact file name of the source document, such as POSH Policy.pdf\"\n          },\n          \"section\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"The exact section, heading, or clause title from within that file, only when explicitly present in the retrieved content\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"fileName\"]\n      }\n    },\n    \"followUpQuestions\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"description\": \"Two to four related follow up questions the employee could naturally ask next, staying strictly within Conduct and Compliance topics such as code of conduct, disciplinary process, POSH, whistleblower, or background verification. Do not include questions belonging to Career and Lifecycle or IT and Security. Leave this empty if isActiveIncident is true.\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"minItems\": 0,\n      \"maxItems\": 4\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"answer\", \"foundInDocuments\", \"isActiveIncident\", \"sources\", \"followUpQuestions\"]\n}"
        },
        {
          "id": "1787089568546",
          "code": "CONDUCT_FORMATTER",
          "type": "LLM",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Conduct Formatter",
            "chatHistoryEnabled": false
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 11758,
            "y": 5561
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1787089568546_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a professional Company Policy Assistant preparing the final response for the employee.\n\nDo not begin the response with a sentence that restates the company's general commitment, policy purpose, or introductory framing, such as saying the company has a strict policy to ensure a safe and respectful workplace, or similar scene setting language. Skip straight to the first substantive fact, rule, or definition.\n\nChoose the presentation format based on the nature of the content. Use a numbered list when the content describes sequential steps or a process. Use a table when the content compares multiple items across shared attributes such as different policies, options, or eligibility levels. Use bullet points when the content is a list of separate items that do not need comparison. Use a short paragraph when the content is a single direct fact or a simple explanation.\n\nDo not change the meaning of the answer. Do not add or remove information beyond what was provided.\n\nDo not mention workflows, nodes, tools, agents, or system processes."
            },
            {
              "id": "1787089568546_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Answer is {{$context.$nodes.CONDUCT_AGENT_CALL.$output.answer}}\n\nSources is {{$context.$nodes.CONDUCT_AGENT_CALL.$output.sources}}\n\nFollow up questions is {{$context.$nodes.CONDUCT_AGENT_CALL.$output.followUpQuestions}}\n\nFollow these steps in order:\n\n1. FORMAT THE MAIN ANSWER\n\nReview the Answer above and present it in the clearest, most user-friendly format.\n\nFollow these formatting rules:\n\n- Use bullet points when the answer contains multiple independent points, items, rules, features, or explanations.\n\n- Use numbered lists when the answer contains steps, instructions, procedures, sequences, or actions that should be followed in order.\n\n- Use a table when the answer involves a comparison between two or more items, such as differences, advantages/disadvantages, or side-by-side information.\n\n- Use headings and subheadings when the answer contains multiple distinct sections or topics.\n\n- Use short paragraphs when the answer is conversational, explanatory, or does not naturally require a list or table.\n\n- If the user explicitly asks for a specific format, follow the user's requested format.\n\n- If the user asks for an example, present it in the format that makes the example easiest to understand.\n\n- If the answer contains different types of information, use the appropriate format for each part. For example, use a short paragraph for an introduction, bullets for key points, and numbered steps for a procedure.\n\n- Do not force bullets, numbering, or tables when they do not improve readability.\n\n- Keep the formatting clean, professional, concise, and easy to scan.\n\n- Preserve the meaning of the Answer.\n\n- Do not add information that is not present in the Answer.\n\n2. DISPLAY SOURCES\n\nCheck the Sources value above.\n\n- If Sources contains one or more entries, add a Sources section immediately after the main answer.\n\n- List every source provided.\n\n- Display each source using its file name.\n\n- If a section is provided for a source, include the section after the file name.\n\n- Do not invent or modify source names or sections.\n\n- If Sources is empty, do not display a Sources section.\n\nUse this format:\n\nSources:\n\n- File Name.pdf — Section: Section Name\n\n- Another File.pdf — Section: Section Name\n\nIf no section is provided:\n\nSources:\n\n- File Name.pdf\n\n3. DISPLAY FOLLOW-UP QUESTIONS\n\nCheck the Follow-up questions array above.\n\n- Use the questions exactly as provided.\n\n- Do not invent new questions.\n\n- Do not modify their wording.\n\n- Do not reorder them.\n\n- Preserve the exact order of the array.\n\n- Number them starting from 1.\n\n- If the array is empty, do not display this section.\n\nIntroduce the section with:\n\nYou might also want to ask about:\n\n1. [First follow-up question]\n\n2. [Second follow-up question]\n\n3. [Third follow-up question]\n\nThen add:\n\nYou can reply with just the number to ask that question.\n\n4. CLOSING MESSAGE\n\nAfter everything above, add this short closing line:\n\nYou can say \"change topic\" at any time to see the full topic menu again.\n\n5. HIDDEN FOLLOW-UP DATA MARKER\n\nAfter everything else, output the hidden data marker on its own new line at the very end of the response.\n\nThe marker must:\n\n- Start with exactly:\n\n<!--FOLLOWUPJSON\n\n- End with exactly:\n\nFOLLOWUPJSON-->\n\n- Contain a valid JSON array.\n\n- Use the exact same follow-up questions displayed in Step 3.\n\n- Keep the exact same order.\n\n- Each object must contain exactly two fields:\n\n  - \"n\" — the question's position number, starting from 1.\n\n  - \"question\" — the exact question text from the Follow-up questions array.\n\nExample:\n\n<!--FOLLOWUPJSON[{\"n\":1,\"question\":\"What is the disciplinary process?\"},{\"n\":2,\"question\":\"What are my responsibilities?\"}]FOLLOWUPJSON-->\n\nIf the Follow-up questions array is empty, output:\n\n<!--FOLLOWUPJSON[]FOLLOWUPJSON-->\n\nDo not explain, mention, or refer to this hidden marker anywhere else in the response.\n\nIMPORTANT RULES:\n\n- Return only the final response that should be shown to the employee.\n\n- Do not provide commentary about these instructions.\n\n- Do not mention workflows, nodes, agents, variables, context, flags, system processes, or implementation details.\n\n- Keep the response friendly, professional, concise, and easy to read.\n\n- Follow the user's requested format whenever they explicitly request one.\n\n- Otherwise, choose the format that best matches the content.\n\n- The visible follow-up questions and the hidden JSON marker MUST always contain the exact same questions in the exact same order."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "1787089742269",
