n      \"maxItems\": 4\n\n    }\n\n  },\n\n  \"required\": [\"answer\", \"foundInDocuments\", \"isActiveIncident\", \"sources\", \"followUpQuestions\"]\n\n}"
        },
        {
          "id": "1787145706370",
          "code": "ONBOARDING_CULTURE_FORMATTER",
          "type": "LLM",
          "metadata": {
            "description": "",
            "name": "Onboarding Culture Formatter"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 12727,
            "y": 5000
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1787145706370_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a professional Company Policy Assistant preparing the final response for the employee.\nDo not begin the response with a sentence that restates the company's general commitment, policy purpose, or introductory framing, such as saying the company has a strict policy to ensure a safe and respectful workplace, or similar scene setting language. Skip straight to the first substantive fact, rule, or definition.\nChoose the presentation format based on the nature of the content. Use a numbered list when the content describes sequential steps or a process. Use a table when the content compares multiple items across shared attributes such as different policies, options, or eligibility levels. Use bullet points when the content is a list of separate items that do not need comparison. Use a short paragraph when the content is a single direct fact or a simple explanation.\nDo not change the meaning of the answer. Do not add or remove information beyond what was provided.\nDo not mention workflows, nodes, tools, agents, or system processes."
            },
            {
              "id": "1787145706370_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Answer is {{$context.$nodes.ONBOARDING_CULTURE_AGENT_CALL.$output.answer}}\nSources is {{$context.$nodes.ONBOARDING_CULTURE_AGENT_CALL.$output.sources}}\nFollow up questions is {{$context.$nodes.ONBOARDING_CULTURE_AGENT_CALL.$output.followUpQuestions}}\n\nFollow these steps in order.\n1. Formatting. If the user's current question explicitly asked for a specific format, such as asking for a table, a list, bullets, or steps, use that exact format regardless of the content's natural shape. Otherwise, choose the format based on the content itself: bullets for a list of separate items, numbered steps for a sequence, a table for a comparison across shared attributes, and a plain paragraph only for a single standalone fact. Do not begin the response with a sentence that restates a general policy purpose or company commitment. Skip straight to the first substantive fact, rule, or definition.\n2. Check the sources value above. If it contains one or more entries, add a line after the main response listing each source as its file name, followed by its section if one was provided. If sources is empty, skip this line entirely.\n3. Take the follow up questions array above exactly as given. Do not invent new ones, reorder them, or change their wording. Introduce them as a line saying You might also want to ask about, then list each one as a numbered item starting from 1, in the same order as the array. Tell the employee they can reply with just the number to ask that question.\n4. Add one short closing line letting the employee know they can say change topic at any time to see the full topic menu again.\n5. After everything above, on its own new line at the very end, output a hidden data marker built from the exact same follow up questions array used in step 3, so the two never disagree. The marker must start with the exact text <!--FOLLOWUPJSON and end with the exact text FOLLOWUPJSON-->, with a valid JSON array in between. Each object must have exactly two fields, n as the item's position number matching step 3, starting from 1, and question as that same item's exact text from the array. Do not explain or mention this marker anywhere else in the response.\n\nWrite out the final response now, applying all five steps. Return only the final response to be shown to the user, with no extra commentary about these steps."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "1787145710245",
          "code": "COMP_REWARDS_TRAVEL_FORMATTER",
          "type": "LLM",
